hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1436","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Bashar, narrated to us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr speaking, On the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the day of breaking the fast or the day of sacrifice, and the greatest of my knowledge is that he said: On the day of breaking the fast, he prayed. He did not pray two rak'ahs before or after. Then he came to the women, and Bilal was with him, and he ordered them to give alms. The woman made her throw her And its loudness"
